CAT = "cusQuant"; SEG = "QNT"
Q = [
 ('If 7x + 4 = 3x + 30, what is x?', 'x = 6.5', ['x = 8.5', 'x = 26', 'x = 2.6'], '7x - 3x = 30 - 4, so 4x = 26 and x = 6.5. Adding the 4 instead of subtracting it gives 4x = 34 and x = 8.5.'),
 ('If y = 2x² - 5x, what is y when x = -3?', '33', ['3', '-3', '51'], '2(-3)² - 5(-3) = 18 + 15 = 33. Forgetting that minus times minus is plus gives 18 - 15 = 3; squaring 2x instead of x gives 36 + 15 = 51.'),
 ('If x + y = 17 and x - y = 5, what is x?', 'x = 11', ['x = 6', 'x = 12', 'x = 22'], 'Adding the equations gives 2x = 22, so x = 11 (and y = 6). 22 is 2x, not x.'),
 ('Which is the factorisation of x² + 2x - 35?', '(x + 7)(x - 5)', ['(x - 7)(x + 5)', '(x + 35)(x - 1)', '(x - 7)(x - 5)'], 'Find two numbers with product -35 and sum +2: +7 and -5. (x - 7)(x + 5) gives -2x, the wrong sign.'),
 ('What are the roots of x² - 9x + 14 = 0?', 'x = 2 or x = 7', ['x = -2 or x = -7', 'x = 1 or x = 14', 'x = -2 or x = 7'], 'x² - 9x + 14 = (x - 2)(x - 7), so x = 2 or x = 7. Check: 2 + 7 = 9 and 2 x 7 = 14.'),
 ('What is (3x + 4)(x - 2) when expanded?', '3x² - 2x - 8', ['3x² + 2x - 8', '3x² - 10x - 8', '3x² - 2x + 8'], '3x² - 6x + 4x - 8 = 3x² - 2x - 8. The middle term is -6x + 4x, not -6x - 4x.'),
 ('What is the value of 16^(3/4)?', '8', ['12', '4', '2'], 'Take the fourth root first, then cube: the fourth root of 16 is 2, and 2³ = 8. 12 comes from multiplying 16 by 3/4.'),
 ('What is the value of log₃ 243?', '5', ['4', '6', '81'], '3⁵ = 3 x 3 x 3 x 3 x 3 = 243, so log₃ 243 = 5. 81 is 243 ÷ 3, and 3⁴ = 81, 3⁶ = 729.'),
 ('y varies directly as x, and y = 21 when x = 6. What is y when x = 10?', 'y = 35', ['y = 25', 'y = 60', 'y = 12.6'], 'y = kx gives k = 21 / 6 = 3.5, so y = 3.5 x 10 = 35. 12.6 comes from treating it as inverse variation.'),
 ('P varies inversely as Q, and P = 12 when Q = 5. What is P when Q = 4?', 'P = 15', ['P = 9.6', 'P = 11', 'P = 20'], 'PQ is constant: 12 x 5 = 60, so P = 60 / 4 = 15. 9.6 comes from treating it as direct variation.'),
 ('An arithmetic progression has first term 7 and common difference 4. What is its 15th term?', '63', ['67', '60', '59'], 'The nth term is a + (n - 1)d = 7 + 14 x 4 = 63. Using 15 x 4 instead of 14 x 4 gives 67.'),
 ('What is the 8th term of the geometric progression 3, 6, 12, ...?', '384', ['768', '192', '48'], 'The nth term is ar^(n - 1) = 3 x 2⁷ = 3 x 128 = 384. Using 2⁸ gives 768.'),
 ('A cleaning fluid is mixed from concentrate and water in the ratio 5 : 3. How much water is in 64 litres of the mixture?', '24 litres', ['40 litres', '19.2 litres', '21 litres'], 'There are 8 parts, so one part is 8 litres and water is 3 x 8 = 24 litres. 40 litres is the concentrate.'),
 ('On a map with scale 1 : 25,000, two border posts are 7.8 cm apart. What is the real distance?', '1.95 km', ['19.5 km', '0.195 km', '195 km'], '7.8 x 25,000 = 195,000 cm = 1,950 m = 1.95 km. Slipping a place when converting cm to km gives 19.5 km.'),
 ("A command collected duty of ₦4 million, ₦6 million, ₦5 million and ₦9 million in four quarters. What fraction of the year's total came in the fourth quarter?", '3/8', ['9/15', '1/4', '5/8'], 'The total is ₦24 million and 9 / 24 = 3/8. 9/15 compares the fourth quarter with the other three quarters combined (4 + 6 + 5 = 15), and 5/8 is the share of the first three quarters.'),
 ('A pie chart shows 240 cargo inspections, of which 54 were machinery. What angle is the machinery sector?', '81°', ['54°', '72°', '90°'], '54 / 240 x 360° = 81°. 54° wrongly uses the count itself as the angle.'),
 ("What is the median of 14, 8, 17, 10, 23 and 13?",
 "13.5", ["14", "14.2", "15.5"],
 "In order: 8, 10, 13, 14, 17, 23. The middle two are 13 and 14, so the median is 13.5. About 14.2 is the mean."),
 ('What is the mode of 4, 7, 7, 2, 9, 4, 7, 5?', '7', ['4', '5.625', '6'], '7 appears three times, more than any other value. 5.625 is the mean and 6 is the median.'),
 ('What is the range of 41, 66, 23, 58 and 35?', '43', ['66', '41', '42'], 'Range = highest - lowest = 66 - 23 = 43. 66 is the highest value and 41 is the median.'),
 ('A sample of 24 parcels has 6 flagged red, 11 flagged amber and 7 flagged green. One is picked at random. What is the probability it is green?', '7/24', ['7/17', '17/24', '1/3'], '7 of the 24 parcels are green, so P = 7/24. 17/24 is the probability of not green; 7/17 wrongly divides by the non-green count.'),
 ('A card is drawn at random from 20 cards numbered 1 to 20. What is the probability that its number is a multiple of 6?', '3/20', ['1/6', '1/5', '7/20'], 'Only 6, 12 and 18 are multiples of 6, so P = 3/20. 1/6 would be true for a die, not for 20 cards.'),
 ('If A = P(1 + rt), what is t?', 't = (A - P)/(Pr)', ['t = (A - P)/r', 't = A/(Pr) - P', 't = (A + P)/(Pr)'], 'Divide by P: A/P = 1 + rt, so rt = (A - P)/P and t = (A - P)/(Pr). Forgetting to divide by P gives (A - P)/r.'),
 ('What is the solution of the inequality 3x - 4 > 11?', 'x > 5', ['x < 5', 'x > 7/3', 'x > 15'], 'Add 4: 3x > 15, then divide by 3: x > 5. Dividing by a positive number does not reverse the sign.'),
 ('In a group of 80 recruits, 35% are women. How many are men?', '52 men', ['28 men', '45 men', '65 men'], '35% of 80 is 28 women, so 80 - 28 = 52 men. 28 is the number of women.'),
]
